# Tailwind, not component SCSS

Use Tailwind utility classes for layout, spacing, sizing, typography, color, and responsive behavior. Both apps load Tailwind 4.

Do **not** add a component stylesheet. No co-located `.scss`, no `styleUrl`, no `styleUrls`, and no `styles:` on `@Component`. Do not create an empty `.scss` file.

```html
<div class="flex items-center gap-4 pb-4">
  <mat-form-field class="w-full md:w-64">
```

```typescript
@Component({
  selector: "app-my-widget",
  templateUrl: "./my-widget.component.html",
  changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush,
})
```

Conditional styling uses class bindings (`[class.hidden]`, `[class]`), not `ngClass` or a stylesheet.

## SCSS only when Tailwind cannot do it

Add component SCSS only for a rule Tailwind cannot express. Keep the file to that rule and comment why Tailwind was not enough. Omit `styleUrl` when the template is entirely Tailwind.

Allowed cases:

- Angular Material internals in **admin-ui**, via `mat.*-overrides` mixins. Not `::ng-deep`.
- Existing app theme files: `styles.scss`, `_theme-colors.scss`. Do not duplicate those tokens in a component file.
- Animations, pseudo-elements, or selectors with no Tailwind equivalent.

Anything else — flex, grid, gap, padding, margin, width, typography, breakpoints (`md:`, `lg:`), one-off wrappers around Material — is Tailwind in the template.
